I tend to spend a fair amount of time pudding farming and I tend
to play neutral chars because the neutral quest artifacts are so
much more appealing. However, I've also developed at taste for
Grayswandir, especially for my two-weaponing characters. So if
one of my puddings is kind enough to drop a HoOA for me, I'm
inclinded to put it on for a while and sacrifice away until I
get Grayswandir as a gift, even though that means I lose all my
divine protection. After receiving Grayswandir and converting
the altar back to neutral, it doesn't take that long to get the
protection back, at least in terms of my typical pudding farming
games. Just remember never to pray while wearing the HoOA and 
your god doesn't seem to mind that much, well modulo the loss
of divine protection.

Although I have no qualms about pudding farming, wishing for
artifacts in general, or breaking any other conducts, there is
something about using the HoOA at ascension time that doesn't
sit quite right with me. Of course, with HP in the 1000's and
AC usually well below -80 that come with pudding farming, I 
usually have the luxury of wandering around the Astral Plane
pretty much at will. In desperate straits, I'm sure I would do
it, but only as a last resort, and wouldn't like it.

